+# Verifying a packaged repair
+
+A passing source test does not update an installed launcher. Production executes the bundled
+`app/cli.js` from the launcher-managed version directory. At launcher startup, `ensurePackagedRuntime`
+validates that directory against `resources/runtime/manifest.json` and replaces a mismatching bundle
+from the package. Updating only the managed copy can therefore be undone by the next launcher start.
+
+Build and install the package containing the repair, using the repository's existing runtime builder
+and manifest validator. Preserve the previous package and configuration for rollback. Activate the
+new package only after active requests have settled. Check the launcher executable path, the package
+and managed manifest bundle IDs, and `/healthz.runtime_entrypoint_sha256` against the SHA-256 of the
+built `app/cli.js`. That health field is captured at process startup; it does not change merely because
+someone overwrites a file while an older daemon remains running. The release version alone cannot
+distinguish two locally modified builds of the same version.
+
